  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `AreaControls` has a new field `outer_offset`. It moves only the outer side of an open boundary (the stock side). `offset` now moves only the picked line, or the whole area when there is no open boundary.\n- The area law (`operation::boundary::resolve`, step 2) reads the two values. When they are equal, it runs the old code path exactly. When they differ on an open boundary, `boundary_turn::grow_apart` grows the kept side by the larger value and clips it to the stock reach grown by `outer_offset`. The far side, shrunk by `offset`, cuts the picked line as before.\n- The Boundary group has two rows: \"Inside boundary offset\" and \"Outside boundary offset\". Each row has its own hint. Both start at 0. The summary says how the outer side moves. It gives a notice when an outside offset has no open boundary to act on.\n- The project file has an optional `outer_offset` key in `area`. An absent key means \"the same as `offset`\". An old file loads its one offset into both values and saves the same bytes. There is no version bump.\n- The stamp hashes `outer_offset` only when it differs from `offset`. The stamp of an old operation does not change.\n- MCP: `set_operation_area` takes `outer_offset`, and the area view shows it. `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and the tool description name it.\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nBoth captures show the Boundary group for a Pocket operation with containment set to On and offsets at 0 mm. The before capture uses the Boundary UI from parent commit `7a626a7f5`. The after capture uses reviewed head `35d28b002cf31a46abc6cbbf45ae2618f2e4b170`.\n\n![Before: Boundary group with one offset row](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/497d536066824a2668d081bef758877515c04a4c/3386/boundary-before.png)\n\n![After: Boundary group with inside and outside offset rows](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/497d536066824a2668d081bef758877515c04a4c/3386/boundary-after.png)\n\nThe images live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch at commit `497d536066824a2668d081bef758877515c04a4c`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe law had one offset step. It grew the kept side of an open boundary by `offset` and shrank the far side by the same value. The one value moved the picked line and the stock line together. A negative value to cut less air also moved the area away from the picked edge.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew pins:\n- `crates/app/tests/area_outer_offset.rs`\n  - `a_negative_outer_offset_pulls_in_the_stock_side_and_keeps_the_picked_edge`: side B of an open boundary on the block's north edge, stock 70 mm, tool R 5. With outer -10 and picked 0, the region edge stays on the chain (y 20) and the outer edge moves from +-45 to +-35. The Pocket feed length drops from 605.8 mm to 315.8 mm. The test also checks the picked offset alone, and a positive picked offset with a negative outer offset.\n  - `one_value_in_both_offsets_is_the_old_law`: equal values -2 move both lines (y 22 and 43). A closed area ignores the outer offset.\n  - `an_old_project_offset_loads_into_both_and_saves_the_same_bytes`: the migration. A file with one `offset` key loads into both values, and save-load-save gives the same bytes. Different values round-trip, and an outer offset of 0 is written.\n  - `the_outer_offset_rides_the_door_and_the_undo`: one undoable `EditOperationParams` step. The door refuses a non-finite value.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/boundary_offset_tests.rs`\n  - `the_boundary_group_has_an_inside_and_an_outside_offset_row`: labels, hints, default 0, an edit of the outside row changes only `outer_offset`, Apply commits it, and undo restores it.\n  - `the_summary_says_an_outside_offset_without_an_open_boundary_does_nothing`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_pick.rs`: `set_operation_area` sets and shows `outer_offset`, and undo resets it.\n\nRed before the fix: the pin did not compile on upstream/main (no field `outer_offset`). With the field and the old law, it failed: `the outer edge moves in: -45 45 45`.\n\nMutations (each put back, pin run, then restored and green again):\n- Old law in step 2 (guard off): red, `the outer edge moves in: -45 45 45`.\n- `grow_apart` grows by `outer` only: red, `the picked edge stays on the chain: 30`.\n- DTO loads an absent key as 0: red, `the one offset loads into both`.\n- Door without `dist(outer_offset)`: red, `a non-finite outer offset is refused`.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 46 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib`: 1426 passed.\n- Heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`, 205 app steps): 0 failed, wall 48.4 min.\n\nExpected-change test: `egui_app::tests::do_not_touch::geometry_boundaries_shows_do_not_touch_controls_rows_and_viewport_marks` failed because the new row moved the last remove button below the 1100 px harness. The harness is now 1200 px tall. The assertions did not change.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Equal offsets run the old code path, so no golden `.cl` or `.nc` changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Face family and a closed ring as the open boundary with two different offsets. They use the same `grow_apart` step, but no test pins them.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill text still lists the old `area` keys. It is a process file, and this PR does not change it. The tool schema describes the new key.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/boundary.rs` grows from 400 to 406 lines. `crates/ui/src/egui_app/boundary.rs` was 437 lines before and is 439 now.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/3338-outer-boundary-offset.md`. The issue asked for a project-file version bump. This PR uses an optional key instead: an old file loads into both values and saves the same bytes, so a bump gives no gain.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3304 (draft i18n) wraps strings in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/boundary.rs` and `crates/ui/src/boundary_summary.rs`. It touches the same files, but a different change (string wrapping). The PR that merges second refreshes.\n- #3283 and #3058 (draft feats) touch `crates/app/src/operation/types/area.rs`. They change the kind list in `area_unsupported`, a different function. The PR that merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Boundary settings have separate inside and outside offsets. The outside offset moves only the stock side of an open boundary, so less air is cut and the picked edge stays in place. An old project keeps its output.\n\nFixes #3338\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
